1
00:00:00,260 --> 00:00:00,940
Phase zero: Collecting Humans Before You Have Anything to Offer Them Here's the problem.

2
00:00:01,560 --> 00:00:07,060
You want to end war and disease. You don't have a nonprofit, registered securities, or a bank account.

3
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:11,900
What you do have is an argument and the audacity to think that might be enough.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,480
This is Phase zero. The goal isn't money (you can't legally accept it yet).

5
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:25,320
The goal is building a database of every human who agrees that dying from preventable causes is a strange thing to tolerate.

6
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:28,620
You're collecting proof of demand before you have a product.

7
00:00:29,260 --> 00:00:36,000
It's a Kickstarter where the reward is "possibly not dying," which is, when you think about it, the most compelling reward

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:44,000
tier in crowdfunding history. The Bootstrapping Problem. Before you can accept donations, you need five zero one (c) (three)

9
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,600
status. Before you can sell bonds, you need S.E.C. registration.

10
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:55,360
Before you can do either, you need a bank account. It's bureaucratic nesting dolls, each one requiring the previous one

11
00:00:55,360 --> 00:01:04,099
to already exist. Humanity has solved this exact problem the same way every time: you collect people first, then point at

12
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:09,920
the crowd when institutions ask "but who wants this?" Abolition, suffrage, civil rights.

13
00:01:10,780 --> 00:01:14,240
Someone wrote down names. The names became bargaining power.

14
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:20,900
The bargaining power became policy. It's almost like democracy works when someone remembers to use it.

15
00:01:22,180 --> 00:01:24,320
Three Types of Allies. People who want to help fall into three categories, each requiring a slightly different dialect of

16
00:01:24,320 --> 00:01:30,200
persuasion. Investors. People who hear "two hundred and seventy-two percent annual return backed by redirected military

17
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:34,410
spending" and immediately open a spreadsheet. Their pupils dilate.

18
00:01:34,840 --> 00:01:38,690
Their pulse quickens. They ask about the term structure. They're not heartless.

19
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:44,520
They just process moral arguments faster when those arguments come with compound interest.

20
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:50,200
They'll wait if the math is good. They will not wait if the math is vibes.

21
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:59,300
Advocates. People motivated by the mission. They share things on social media, write to politicians, volunteer time, and

22
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:05,920
donate money they probably shouldn't. They are, frankly, the only reason your species has ever improved anything.

23
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:10,919
Without them, the spreadsheet people would still be optimizing returns on the slave trade.

24
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:18,920
Give them specific actions they can take right now. Telling someone "care about this" without giving them something to do

25
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:27,100
is how you manufacture apathy. I have watched four thousand two hundred and ninety-seven years of humans being told to "raise

26
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:33,540
awareness." Awareness has been raised. The awareness is just sitting there, fully raised, doing nothing.

27
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:42,760
Institutional Partners. Organizations (nonprofits, research institutions, health agencies) that already work on pieces of

28
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:43,880
this problem. They have infrastructure, credibility, and donor bases.

29
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:46,840
You have a framework that could make their existing work more effective.

30
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:53,940
This is a trade, not a favor. Approach it like one. Nobody wants to be "partnered with" by someone who clearly just wants

31
00:02:53,940 --> 00:03:01,000
their mailing list. Institutions are territorial in the way that dogs are territorial, except dogs eventually stop barking.

32
00:03:02,260 --> 00:03:08,220
Phase Zero Targets. One hundred thousand plus registered supporters across all three categories.

33
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:13,260
One thousand plus qualified investors with stated investment ranges.

34
00:03:14,060 --> 00:03:17,360
One hundred plus institutional partners with expressed interest.

35
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:24,280
One billion dollars plus in stated investment demand (registered, not committed).

36
00:03:25,420 --> 00:03:32,690
This database is your ammunition for everything that follows: Five zero one c three applications ("here are our supporters").

37
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:38,740
S.E.C. registration ("here is market demand"). Political meetings ("here are your constituents").

38
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:44,420
Platform launch ("here are your users"). Bureaucrats don't respond to arguments.

39
00:03:44,980 --> 00:03:48,820
They respond to evidence that other people already responded to arguments.

40
00:03:49,540 --> 00:03:54,000
It's like a restaurant: nobody wants to eat there until other people are already eating there.

41
00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:58,600
Your entire civilization runs on this principle, and nobody admits it.

42
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:05,970
You literally invented a word for it ("social proof") so you could study it in universities instead of just feeling embarrassed.

43
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:14,280
Getting Started. One. Build three registration forms (investors, advocates, partners).

44
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:19,720
Takes twenty minutes. Two. Put up a website. The forms and the argument.

45
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:25,140
It does not need to be pretty. No movement in history was stopped because the font was wrong.

46
00:04:25,580 --> 00:04:31,980
Three. Start telling people. Social media, Reddit, forums, conferences, your dentist.

47
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:35,940
Especially your dentist. You're already trapped there. They can't leave either.

48
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:41,220
It's the perfect recruiting environment. Four. Send monthly updates.

49
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:49,200
Real progress, real numbers, real timeline. "Three thousand two hundred and forty-seven registered investors representing

50
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:57,860
one hundred and eighty million dollars in early-stage retail interest, before institutional commitments" beats "the movement

51
00:04:57,860 --> 00:05:02,760
is growing!" because adults prefer arithmetic to enthusiasm.

52
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:11,460
The military-industrial complex has a sixty-five-year head start, unlimited budgets, and thousands of lobbyists.

53
00:05:12,260 --> 00:05:16,800
You have a spreadsheet and an argument. Historically, that's been enough.

54
00:05:17,420 --> 00:05:20,840
(It shouldn't be. But your species is weird like that.).
